<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Bourbon</h1><p class="st-meta">1327 CE – 1527 CE · capital Moulins</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The central French duchy of a Capetian branch whose last great duke betrayed Francis I and whose cousins later became kings of France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The lords of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a> had held the Bourbonnais since the 10th century. In 1272 the heiress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beatrice-of-bourbon">Beatrice of Bourbon</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-count-of-clermont">Robert of Clermont</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX</a>, and in 1327 Charles IV raised the barony to a duchy for their son Louis I, creating the Capetian house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moulins">Moulins</a> and gathered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-forez">Forez</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-beaujeu">Beaujolais</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-auvergne">Auvergne</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-la-marche">La Marche</a> through marriage and inheritance, making their lands one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France's</a> largest princely blocs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-duke-of-bourbon">Louis II</a>, called the Good Duke, was a model crusading prince. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-france">Anne of France</a> and her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-duke-of-bourbon">Peter II</a> governed the kingdom during the minority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france">Charles VIII</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-duke-of-bourbon">Charles III</a>, constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, fell out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a>, who claimed his lands; he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in 1523 and was killed leading the sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1527. His lands were confiscated and joined to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>, but a younger <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a> line gave France <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="Duchy of Bourbon" width="320" height="308"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bourbounnais_in_France_(1789).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1327 CE – 1527 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Moulins</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Louis I of Bourbon, Louis II of Bourbon, Charles III of Bourbon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bourbonnais, Lordship of Bourbon</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1427&amp;focus=duchy-of-bourbon" aria-label="Duchy of Bourbon on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4758 541 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Bourbon lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5078 797L5054 728M5078 797L5100 822M5078 797L5153 869"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5100 822h0M5153 869h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5078 797h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5078 797h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Moulins. <a href="/atlas?year=1427&amp;focus=duchy-of-bourbon">On the